WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.560
The school moves from Saturday cardiac arrest into Sunday care of the deteriorating patient, acute coronary syndrome, perfusion assessment and live STEMI notification. This lesson follows that sequence rather than adding an unrelated anatomy chapter.
学校从周六心脏骤停，转到周日恶化患者、急性冠脉综合征、灌注评估及STEMI现场通知练习。本课依此顺序，不另塞无关解剖章节。

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:31.272
A patient with a pulse may still be close to arrest. Your opportunity is to identify the changing physiology and support the patient before circulation fails, while arranging the help and receiving pathway the situation needs.
有脉搏仍可能临近骤停。机会在于循环失败前识别生理变化并支持患者，同时安排情境需要的支援及接收路径。

00:00:31.272 --> 00:00:42.912
Use the previous rhythm and twelve-lead teaching as tools, not as a reason to repeat a whole monitor chapter. Here the question is what the trace and patient together require next.
把此前心律及十二导联知识作为工具，不是再重复整章监护。本课要问的是：记录结合患者后，下一步需要什么。

00:00:42.912 --> 00:00:55.416
The original cases teach the school objectives without completing school assessments. The original PCP PowerPoints and actual skill rubric are not recovered, so their unseen instructions are not invented.
原创病例用于教授学校目标，不代做学校考核。原始PCP幻灯片及实际技能评分表尚未取得，所以不会编造其中未见指令。

00:00:55.416 --> 00:01:11.472
Peri-arrest describes unstable physiology around the time of an arrest, including the period before it. New confusion, syncope, ischemic discomfort, poor oxygenation or pulmonary edema can warn of imminent deterioration.
骤停前后不稳定生理都属于peri-arrest，包括骤停之前。新混乱、晕厥、缺血不适、氧合差或肺水肿，都可警示即将恶化。

00:01:11.472 --> 00:01:27.504
Use serial observations. A pressure of one hundred may represent a major fall for this patient, while a slow rate can be well tolerated in someone else. Neither a single cuff threshold nor a rhythm label describes the whole circulation.
应使用连续观察。收缩压一百对这位患者可能已大降，另一个人的慢心率却可能耐受良好。单次袖带阈值或心律名称，都不能描述整个循环。

00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:39.672
A quieter patient is not automatically better. Exhaustion with smaller breaths and declining awareness may be respiratory failure, even if the earlier distress looked more dramatic.
患者安静下来不自动表示好转。疲惫、呼吸变浅及意识下降可能是呼吸衰竭，即使之前挣扎看着更明显。

00:01:39.672 --> 00:01:52.176
State the working problem aloud: deteriorating perfusion with a pulse, or inadequate ventilation, for example. That statement aligns the team before the exact diagnosis is settled.
应把工作问题说出来，例如仍有脉搏但灌注恶化，或通气不足。确切诊断未定前，这句话就能让团队方向一致。

00:01:52.176 --> 00:02:06.912
Approach safely and assess responsiveness, airway, breathing and circulation. Correct an immediate threat with the least invasive effective trained intervention; do not finish a history while ventilation fails.
安全接近后评反应、气道、呼吸及循环。即时威胁要用受训范围内最少侵入且有效的方法纠正，不能在通气失败时坚持问完病史。

00:02:06.912 --> 00:02:20.712
Delegate tasks by actual capability. One partner can gather a focused history while another obtains observations or prepares an ECG, as long as someone continues to watch the patient and coordinate priorities.
按真实能力分工。一人可问重点病史，另一人取观察或准备ECG，但必须有人持续观察患者并协调优先级。

00:02:20.712 --> 00:02:36.048
Bring movement equipment to the patient and minimize avoidable exertion. Choose position according to breathing, perfusion, airway protection and tolerance instead of requiring every cardiac patient to sit or lie in one fixed angle.
应把移动器材带到患者身边，减少可避免用力。体位依呼吸、灌注、气道保护和耐受选择，不要求所有心脏患者固定坐或卧某个角度。

00:02:36.048 --> 00:02:48.336
Make the conveyance and additional-resource decision early and keep reassessing it. A needed intervention and a transport plan are coordinated actions, not mutually exclusive choices.
尽早决定转运及额外资源，并继续复评。必要干预与转运计划需要协调，并非二选一。

00:02:48.336 --> 00:03:03.120
Coronary flow supplies the working myocardium. Plaque disruption with thrombosis is a major acute mechanism, while spasm, severe anemia, low flow and increased demand can create other supply-demand problems.
冠脉血流供应工作心肌。斑块破坏并形成血栓是重要急性机制，而痉挛、严重贫血、低血流及需求增加也可造成其他供需问题。

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:18.360
Pain, fear and sympathetic stimulation can increase rate, force and vascular load. Calm communication and reducing exertion support care, but reassurance alone cannot restore an occluded coronary artery.
疼痛、恐惧及交感刺激可增加心率、力量及血管负荷。平静沟通与减少用力有帮助，但安慰本身不能打开堵塞冠脉。

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:30.696
Ischemia can impair both electrical stability and pumping. The patient may develop a dangerous rhythm, pulmonary congestion, reduced output or more than one complication at once.
缺血可同时损害电稳定及泵功能。患者可能出现危险心律、肺淤血、低心排，也可多个并发症同时发生。

00:03:30.696 --> 00:03:42.528
This is why medication pain relief is only one endpoint. You must still follow perfusion, breathing, the ECG and the plan for definitive evaluation or reperfusion.
所以止痛只是一个终点。仍要跟踪灌注、呼吸、ECG，以及确定性评估或再灌注计划。

00:03:42.528 --> 00:03:57.216
The school Week 5 cardiovascular video offers a broad disease-family map. Use it to generate a differential, then return to the patient, the ECG and current service guidance. It is not a bedside diagnosis checklist.
学校第5周心血管视频提供疾病家族概览。可用它扩展鉴别诊断，再回到患者、ECG及现行机构指引；它不是床边诊断清单。

00:03:57.216 --> 00:04:13.608
Congestion, pain, fatigue, syncope and abnormal pulses can arise through different mechanisms. Ask what the finding means for flow, oxygen supply, rhythm or cardiac filling rather than equating a symptom with one disease name.
淤血、疼痛、疲劳、晕厥和异常脉搏可能由不同机制造成。应问发现对血流、氧供应、心律或心脏充盈意味着什么，而不是把症状等同某个病名。

00:04:13.608 --> 00:04:28.968
Correct the video before memorizing it: PFO is not defined as a fixed left-to-right shunt, and transposition is not caused by both fetal connections failing to close. The bilingual guide gives the corrected anatomy and references.
记忆前先纠正视频：PFO不能定义为固定左向右分流；大动脉转位也不是由两个胎儿交通都未闭合导致。中英阅读指南提供正确解剖及来源。

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:42.120
Keep the operational layer separate. This lesson teaches recognition and communication; current BCEHS pathways, actual authorization and appropriate consultation determine field actions.
必须区分临床操作层。本课教识别和沟通；现场行动由现行BCEHS路径、实际权限及必要咨询决定。

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:57.120
Acute coronary syndrome includes unstable angina, non-ST-elevation infarction and ST-elevation infarction. Stable predictable angina is not itself included, despite a contradictory early box in the main text.
急性冠脉综合征包括不稳定心绞痛、非ST抬高梗死及ST抬高梗死。稳定可预测心绞痛本身不属于其中，主教材前面一个框对此有矛盾。

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:10.152
Symptoms alone usually cannot distinguish the acute categories. A nondiagnostic ECG does not exclude ACS, and an NSTEMI can still have significant ECG abnormalities.
症状本身通常不能区分这些急性类别。ECG未达到诊断性不能排除ACS，NSTEMI也仍可有重要ECG异常。

00:05:10.152 --> 00:05:23.976
STEMI and NSTEMI are not reliable synonyms for a completely blocked versus partly blocked artery in every patient. Use the actual clinical and ECG pathway, not that simplified anatomical shortcut.
对每名患者，STEMI与NSTEMI都不能可靠等同完全堵塞及部分堵塞。应使用真实临床与ECG路径，而非简化解剖捷径。

00:05:23.976 --> 00:05:37.464
The prehospital task is recognition, safe early treatment and connection to the appropriate receiving service. Do not postpone those actions until an unavailable biomarker result resolves the terminology.
院前任务是识别、安全早期治疗及连接适当接收机构。不能等没有条件获得的生物标志物先把术语区分清，才开始行动。

00:05:37.464 --> 00:05:54.264
Start with an open question and establish true onset and progression. Chest pressure, breathlessness, nausea, weakness, diaphoresis or syncope can be cardiac symptoms; do not require a classic clenched-fist chest-pain story.
先开放提问，确定真实起病及进展。胸压、气促、恶心、虚弱、出汗或晕厥都可能是心脏症状，不能要求先有典型握拳胸痛故事。

00:05:54.264 --> 00:06:07.296
Ask what was taken, how much and when, including dispatcher-assisted ASA, home nitrate and medicines borrowed from another person. A listed prescription is not proof of today’s dose.
要问服过什么、多少及何时，包括调度指导ASA、家用硝酸酯及借别人药。清单上的处方不证明今日实际服量。

00:06:07.296 --> 00:06:23.016
Ask sensitively about PDE5 medicines, explaining the possible interaction. Include beta blockers, calcium-channel blockers, anticoagulants, kidney disease and recent illness when these change the risk or likely mechanism.
应敏感询问PDE5药并解释相互作用。若会改变风险或可能机制，还需问β阻滞剂、钙阻滞剂、抗凝、肾病及近期疾病。

00:06:23.016 --> 00:06:37.008
Clarify an allergy by the actual reaction, and distinguish it from an expected side effect. Obtain critical facts first; the remaining history can continue without delaying urgent support or conveyance.
过敏要问真实反应，并与预期副作用区分。先取关键事实，其余病史可继续，但不能因此延误紧急支持或转运。

00:06:37.008 --> 00:06:53.016
Combine mentation, pulse quality, pressure, respiratory effort and skin findings. Look for a pattern of low output, congestion or another threat rather than accepting normal saturation as proof of normal perfusion.
结合意识、脉搏力量、血压、呼吸功及皮肤，寻找低输出、淤血或其他威胁模式，不能把饱和度正常当灌注正常的证明。

00:06:53.016 --> 00:07:07.464
Crackles, wheeze, neck-vein changes and edema provide useful context. None independently proves a single diagnosis, and a patient can have serious disease without all the expected findings.
湿啰音、喘鸣、颈静脉改变及水肿都提供背景，但没有一项独立证明单病，重要疾病也不一定全部预期表现都有。

00:07:07.464 --> 00:07:22.344
Assess relevant pulses and asymmetry without compressing both carotids. A pulse-strength grade is descriptive, not an exact cuff pressure. Do not keep repeating a difficult measurement while an obvious primary threat goes untreated.
评相关脉搏及不对称时，不得同时压双颈动脉。脉搏力量分级只是描述，不是确切袖带血压。不能为反复测困难读数而不处理明显主要威胁。

00:07:22.344 --> 00:07:35.352
Write down the actual findings and times. Rechecking after moving the patient is especially important because exertion, position and interrupted equipment can change the physiology and measurement.
应记真实发现及时间。移动后尤其要复查，因为用力、体位及设备中断都会改变生理或测量。

00:07:35.352 --> 00:07:47.952
Chest symptoms are not automatically ACS. Aortic disease, pulmonary embolism, pneumothorax and other conditions can resemble it and may change the safety of a planned intervention.
胸部症状不自动等于ACS。主动脉病、肺栓塞、气胸等可相似，并可能改变计划干预的安全性。

00:07:47.952 --> 00:08:05.136
Use onset, associated neurologic or limb findings, breathing and circulation to maintain a sensible differential. Equal arm pressures, reproducible discomfort or a nondiagnostic ECG cannot individually exclude the dangerous alternatives.
要结合起病、伴随神经肢体发现、呼吸和循环，保持合理鉴别。双臂血压相同、可触发不适或ECG无诊断性，单独都不能排除危险替代病因。

00:08:05.136 --> 00:08:18.024
Do not force every finding into one diagnosis. Chronic edema can coexist with a new coronary problem, and a fast pulse may be responding to blood loss rather than causing the illness.
不能把全部发现硬塞成一个诊断。慢性水肿可与新冠脉问题并存，快脉也可能在响应失血而非造成疾病。

00:08:18.024 --> 00:08:29.232
Report the working suspicion and important uncertainty early. Support immediate needs while the receiving pathway provides investigations that cannot be completed in the field.
应尽早报告工作怀疑及重要不确定性。在接收路径进行现场无法完成的检查时，先支持即时需要。

00:08:29.232 --> 00:08:44.856
Use the Week Three landmark sequence and the actual trained equipment. A twelve-lead recording uses ten electrodes. Limb or chest-lead substitution can create misleading changes and cannot be repaired by a confident interpretation.
使用第3周定位顺序及实际受训器材。十二导联记录用十个电极，肢体或胸导联乱替换会制造误导改变，再自信的解释也无法修复。

00:08:44.856 --> 00:08:59.736
Position and expose respectfully, prepare the skin and reduce avoidable movement or cable tension. Check the actual tracing for baseline disturbance, disconnected leads and unusual patterns that might reflect a placement problem.
应尊重地安排体位及暴露，准备皮肤，减少可避免运动和线缆牵拉。实际查看基线干扰、导联脱落及可能由定位造成的异常模式。

00:08:59.736 --> 00:09:13.776
Record the symptom state and time, including whether treatment was given before acquisition. A treatment-related change can matter, but needed life support must not be withheld merely to preserve an untreated ECG.
记录症状状态及时间，包括采集前是否已治疗。治疗相关改变可能重要，但不能只为保留未治疗ECG就扣住必要生命支持。

00:09:13.776 --> 00:09:24.960
If the trace is not interpretable, correct the likely cause promptly while care continues. A printout with twelve labels is not automatically a diagnostic recording.
记录不能解释时，应在持续照护中迅速纠正可能原因。有十二个标签的打印纸，不自动等于诊断性记录。

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:39.936
The saved Week Three module defines its under-three-minute acquisition drill from patient contact to a readable diagnostic ECG. Week Five calls for timed acquisitions but does not provide a separate recovered timing rubric.
保存的第3周模块将三分钟内采集练习定义为从患者接触到可读诊断性ECG。第5周要求限时采集，但没有取得另一份计时评分细则。

00:09:39.936 --> 00:09:53.064
Carry the skill forward as a practice target, not as permission to abandon immediate care. Assign tasks before the timer starts and keep airway, ventilation and perfusion support running in parallel.
可把此技能作为本周练习目标，不是放弃即时照护的许可。计时前先分工，气道、通气及灌注支持应并行。

00:09:53.064 --> 00:10:06.264
Stop the practice clock at an actual usable recording, not the first button press or first printed artifact. Record the delay reason honestly and improve the workflow instead of changing the start time.
练习时钟应在真正可用记录时结束，不是在第一次按键或打印伪差时。要诚实记录延误原因并改流程，不能改起点。

00:10:06.264 --> 00:10:19.152
If physiology deteriorates, the patient takes priority and the team announces the change. A fast ECG that was obtained at the cost of essential care is not a successful performance.
若生理恶化，患者优先，团队需宣布变化。牺牲必要照护换来的快速ECG，不算成功表现。

00:10:19.152 --> 00:10:32.616
The school asks you to recognize inferior STEMI rapidly. Inspect leads Two, Three and a V F as a contiguous group, in a patient with compatible symptoms and a technically useful recording.
学校要求快速识别下壁STEMI。应在症状相符且技术有用的记录上，把II、III及aVF作为相邻区域一起看。

00:10:32.616 --> 00:10:51.120
An illustrative criterion is new ST elevation of at least one millimeter in two contiguous inferior leads in the appropriate clinical setting. The more complex V Two and V Three thresholds belong to the earlier lead-specific lesson, not a one-millimeter rule for every lead.
适当临床背景下，一个示例标准是两个相邻下壁导联新ST抬高至少一毫米。V2和V3更复杂阈值归此前导联特定课程，不能把一毫米变成每个导联通用规则。

00:10:51.120 --> 00:11:05.640
Look for reciprocal clues and evolving changes, but do not require a reciprocal pattern before reporting concern. Mimics and baseline abnormalities mean that the whole trace and clinical picture still need trained interpretation.
应寻找镜像线索及演变，但不能非有镜像才报告怀疑。模拟改变和基线异常意味着仍需受训解释整份记录及临床情况。

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:19.320
Inferior ischemia can affect nodal function and coexist with right-sided involvement. Slow rate and falling pressure are patient findings to act on, not merely interesting additions to the ECG label.
下壁缺血可影响结点功能并并存右侧受累。慢心率和血压下降是需行动的患者发现，不只是ECG名称后的有趣附加项。

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:35.664
Consider additional right-sided or posterior assessment through the trained pathway when the clinical and standard ECG findings suggest it. Extra lead positions must be accurate and clearly labeled, not mixed with a standard recording without explanation.
临床及标准ECG提示时，可通过受训流程考虑额外右侧或后壁评估。额外导联要准确并明确标注，不能无说明混成标准记录。

00:11:35.664 --> 00:11:50.448
An inferior pattern alone does not prove right ventricular infarction. Conversely, a single absent clue does not erase concern in a hypotensive patient. Integrate the trace, perfusion and medication screen.
下壁模式本身不证明右室梗死；反过来，低血压患者缺一条线索也不能抹去怀疑。应整合记录、灌注及药物筛查。

00:11:50.448 --> 00:12:03.816
Do not keep delaying notification until every possible lead has been obtained. Send or describe the useful information already available, explain what remains uncertain and coordinate further acquisition if appropriate.
不能为取得所有可能导联而不断延迟通知。应先传或描述已有有用信息，说明不确定之处，并按需要协调后续采集。

00:12:03.816 --> 00:12:16.800
A lead-based prediction is not a substitute for ongoing patient assessment. Changes in consciousness, breathing or pulse still drive immediate priorities even while the ECG work continues.
根据导联预测不能替代持续评估。即使仍在取ECG，意识、呼吸或脉搏改变仍决定即时重点。

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:31.896
Give a concise identity and time sequence: onset or last symptom-free time when known, first contact, ECG time and expected arrival. Distinguish confirmed facts from estimates or collateral reports.
预警要简明给身份及时间顺序：已知起病或最后无症状时间、首次接触、ECG时间及预计抵达，并区分确定事实、估计和旁证。

00:12:31.896 --> 00:12:46.560
State suspected STEMI territory together with the patient state, such as inferior changes with bradycardia and hypoperfusion. Include relevant treatment, actual response and why a usual intervention was withheld.
说明疑似STEMI区域及患者状态，例如下壁改变伴过缓和低灌注。包括相关治疗、实际反应，以及为何未给通常考虑的干预。

00:12:46.560 --> 00:13:02.760
The school case asks for a PCI-center bypass pre-alert. In real practice, eligibility, geography, instability and regional agreements determine the destination. Do not announce a universal bypass without confirming the actual pathway.
学校病例要求PCI中心绕行预警；真实工作中，资格、地理、不稳定程度及区域约定决定目的地。不能不确认实际路径就宣布人人通用绕行。

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:16.824
Transmit an interpretable trace where the system supports it and confirm receipt or the next communication step. A sent message is not proof that a cath team accepted activation or that responsibility has transferred.
系统支持时应传可解释记录，并确认接收或下一沟通步骤。消息已发不证明导管团队已接受启动，也不表示责任已转交。

00:13:16.824 --> 00:13:31.344
ASA inhibits platelet cyclooxygenase irreversibly and reduces thromboxane activity. Its purpose in appropriate suspected ACS is not analgesic proof, venodilation or direct clot dissolution.
ASA不可逆抑制血小板环氧化酶并减少血栓烷活性。适当疑似ACS使用时，目的不是通过止痛证明诊断、扩静脉或直接溶栓。

00:13:31.344 --> 00:13:45.576
Check prior intake, the actual allergy reaction and relevant bleeding concerns. ASA-triggered respiratory reaction matters, but an asthma diagnosis alone is not proof that the patient is allergic to ASA.
需核已服量、真实过敏反应及相关出血问题。ASA诱发呼吸反应重要，但哮喘诊断本身不证明对ASA过敏。

00:13:45.576 --> 00:14:03.888
The saved BC examination guide specifies one hundred sixty milligrams; the checked current service monograph specifies one hundred sixty-two milligrams chewed and swallowed. The main text has a wider older range. Keep the required source explicit rather than combining doses.
保存的BC考试指南写160 mg，核对的现行机构专论写162 mg嚼服咽下，主教材还有较宽旧范围。必须明确所用来源，不能把剂量合并。

00:14:03.888 --> 00:14:17.592
Follow the applicable protocol for prior doses and contraindications. The patient still needs monitoring, reassessment and appropriate conveyance after ASA; a tablet cannot complete the coronary pathway.
既往剂量及禁忌应按适用规程处理。ASA后仍需监护、复评及适当转运，一片药不能完成冠脉路径。

00:14:17.592 --> 00:14:29.832
A patient may have inadequate tissue oxygen delivery from poor flow or anemia despite a reassuring saturation. A low-quality peripheral signal during shock may also be unreliable.
患者可能因低血流或贫血而氧输送不足，即使饱和度看着不错。休克时质量差的外周信号也可能不可靠。

00:14:29.832 --> 00:14:44.088
Provide oxygen according to the applicable clinical guidance and the patient’s need, while assessing ventilation and perfusion. Increasing oxygen flow cannot replace ventilating a patient whose breaths are inadequate.
氧疗应依适用临床指导及需要，同时评估通气灌注。患者呼吸不足时，加大氧流不能替代通气。

00:14:44.088 --> 00:14:57.912
The older Nancy ninety-to-ninety-four-percent band differs from checked current local guidance. Keep these source targets labeled; do not invent a universal average or a rigid cap that prevents correction of hypoxemia.
Nancy旧90%至94%范围与核对的现行当地指导不同，需分来源标明，不能自行平均，也不能设一个阻碍纠正低氧的死上限。

00:14:57.912 --> 00:15:13.704
Post-ROSC hyperoxia precautions are covered in the separate arrest-transition lecture. They do not justify withholding needed oxygen during active resuscitation or ignoring a deteriorating patient because one saturation appears normal.
ROSC后高氧防范已在骤停转换讲座单列；它不允许复苏中扣住所需氧，也不允许因一次饱和度正常就忽略患者恶化。

00:15:13.704 --> 00:15:27.408
At usual lower doses, nitroglycerin predominantly dilates veins and reduces preload. This may relieve selected ischemic discomfort but can reduce output when the circulation depends on limited filling.
常见低剂量硝酸甘油主要扩静脉、降低前负荷，可缓解部分缺血不适，但充盈已不足且循环依赖它时，也可降低输出。

00:15:27.408 --> 00:15:42.936
The checked current PCP monograph requires systolic pressure at least one hundred ten and rate between fifty and one hundred fifty, with no significant hypoperfusion. Passing the numbers alone does not clear the other contraindications.
核对的现行PCP专论要求收缩压至少110、心率50至150，且没有重要低灌注。仅数字过关，不表示其他禁忌已清除。

00:15:42.936 --> 00:15:58.632
Ask about sildenafil or vardenafil within twenty-four hours and tadalafil within forty-eight hours under that monograph. These medicines may be used for more than erectile dysfunction, so ask respectfully and explain the interaction.
按该专论，要问24小时内西地那非或伐地那非、48小时内他达拉非。这些药用途不止勃起功能障碍，应尊重询问并解释相互作用。

00:15:58.632 --> 00:16:16.848
The contraindication list also includes right-sided acute infarction, uncorrected hypovolemia, tamponade and other specific conditions. Inferior ischemia requires caution and assessment for right-sided involvement; pain severity does not override the screen.
禁忌还包括右侧急性梗死、未纠正低血容量、压塞等具体情况。下壁缺血需谨慎并评估右侧受累，疼痛严重也不能越过筛查。

00:16:16.848 --> 00:16:30.360
Follow the serial circuit. If right-sided filling or pumping is already limited, less blood may reach the left ventricle. Additional venodilation can reduce filling further and worsen systemic output.
沿串联循环推理：右侧充盈或泵血已受限时，到左室的血可能更少；额外静脉舒张可进一步减少充盈，并恶化体循环输出。

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:45.408
The school case combines inferior changes, a rate of forty-four and a pressure of eighty-eight over fifty. Both the pressure and rate fail the current PCP nitrate screen, even before the additional concern about right-sided involvement.
学校病例组合下壁改变、心率44及血压88/50。即使先不谈额外右侧受累担忧，血压和心率也都不符合现行PCP硝酸酯筛查。

00:16:45.408 --> 00:17:01.296
Do not simplify this into every inferior infarct is identical or every patient needs a fluid bolus. Congestion, volume status, breathing and the likely mechanism still determine the appropriate support and consultation.
不能简化成每个下壁梗死都相同，或人人都需推液。淤血、容量状态、呼吸及可能机制，仍决定适当支持及咨询。

00:17:01.296 --> 00:17:15.816
Withhold an excluded intervention, explain why, protect immediate physiology and arrange appropriate help and conveyance. A contraindication is a decision to choose safer care, not a decision to do nothing.
应不做被排除的干预并解释原因，同时保护即时生理、安排适当支援转运。禁忌意味着选择更安全照护，不是什么也不做。

00:17:15.816 --> 00:17:30.936
The current monograph lists a point-four-milligram sublingual dose at three-to-five-minute intervals; C Zero One names four to five minutes. These are an identified source difference, not a new combined interval invented by this course.
现行专论列舌下0.4 mg、三至五分钟间隔，C01写四至五分钟。这是已识别来源差异，不会由本课发明一个合并间隔。

00:17:30.936 --> 00:17:44.472
The same current monograph requires prior CliniCall consultation without a prior prescription or when more than three doses are needed. The older main-text three-to-six-dose wording does not remove that requirement.
同一现行专论要求无既往处方或需超过三剂时事先CliniCall咨询，主教材旧三至六剂措辞不会取消此要求。

00:17:44.472 --> 00:17:58.368
Check pressure, rate, actual perfusion and relevant symptoms before every authorized repeat. A previous tolerated dose does not guarantee safety after volume loss, rhythm change or a falling pressure.
每次获授权重复前，均要核血压、心率、实际灌注及相关症状。失液、心律变化或血压下降后，上一剂耐受不能保证下一剂安全。

00:17:58.368 --> 00:18:09.840
Reassess pain and adverse effects without using headache or sublingual burning as a potency test. Do not remain on scene merely to finish a fixed number of symptom-relief doses.
复评疼痛及不良效应，但不能用头痛或舌下灼感作为药效检验，也不能只为完成固定次数止痛剂量而留现场。

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:24.624
Hypotension can arise through several mechanisms. Assess volume loss, congestion, pump function clues, obstruction, medicines and the clinical trend before assuming the ventricle simply needs more fluid.
低血压可由多种机制造成。假设心室只是缺液前，应评容量丢失、淤血、泵功能线索、梗阻、药物及临床趋势。

00:18:24.624 --> 00:18:38.400
An indicated fluid intervention needs a patient-specific authorized plan and a response check. In suspected cardiogenic shock, the current shock guideline recommends consultation for care planning before treatment.
有指征补液需患者特定获授权计划及反应检查。疑心源性休克时，现行休克指南建议治疗前咨询照护计划。

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:51.600
Watch mentation, pulse, pressure, breathing and congestion, not only the amount that entered the line. More volume can improve filling or make lung function worse depending on the underlying problem.
应看意识、脉、血压、呼吸及淤血，不能只看多少液体进了管。依原问题不同，加量可能改善充盈，也可能恶化肺功能。

00:18:51.600 --> 00:19:04.392
Establish access when appropriate without delaying definitive care. A patent IV is preparation, not a requirement to give a large bolus or evidence that the cause has been corrected.
适当时建立通路，但不能延误确定性照护。静脉通畅只是准备，不要求一定大推，也不证明病因已纠正。

00:19:04.392 --> 00:19:17.184
A low rate may be normal for an individual, medication-related or a sign of disease. Assess the patient’s baseline, symptoms and perfusion rather than treating every rate below sixty.
低心率可属个人正常、药物相关或疾病信号，应看基线、症状及灌注，不能每个低于60都治疗。

00:19:17.184 --> 00:19:32.184
Current C Zero Two uses a below-fifty framework and emphasizes clinical endpoints rather than a target number alone. A relatively well-perfused patient may need monitoring and conveyance without immediate rate-specific treatment.
现行C02使用低于50框架，并强调临床终点，不只追心率目标。灌注尚好者可能需监护转运，但不立即专门改心率。

00:19:32.184 --> 00:19:45.360
Search for hypoxia, ischemia, vagal influence, medicines or overdose, kidney disease and electrolyte risk. Correcting a cause can be more important than making a monitor rate look normal.
应找低氧、缺血、迷走影响、药物过量、肾病及电解质风险。纠正病因可能比让屏幕心率正常更重要。

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:55.704
Continue to watch for a changing state. Stable describes the present assessment, not a guarantee about the next ten minutes or permission to leave the patient unobserved.
仍需观察状态变化。稳定描述当前评估，不保证接下来十分钟，也不允许无人观察。

00:19:55.704 --> 00:20:09.504
A slow rhythm with worsening mentation, hypotension or other hypoperfusion is a different clinical state. Provide effective primary support and request the appropriate advanced help without waiting for complete rhythm certainty.
慢心律伴意识、血压或其他灌注恶化，是不同临床状态。应有效支持主要问题并请求适当高级支援，不等心律完全确定。

00:20:09.504 --> 00:20:25.800
Atropine, epinephrine infusion and transcutaneous pacing are advanced service interventions, not independent PCP actions created by this lesson. Preparation and assistance still matter, including equipment and accurate observations.
阿托品、肾上腺素输注及经皮起搏属机构高级干预，不是本课创造的PCP独立动作；器材及准确观察等准备协助仍重要。

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:41.424
The main text lists atropine point-five milligrams, the PHARM candidate one milligram, and the checked local monograph point-six milligrams for adult bradycardia. Keep those source regimens separate instead of choosing or averaging a dose.
主教材成人过缓阿托品写0.5 mg，PHARM候选本1 mg，核对的本地专论0.6 mg。必须分清来源方案，不能自选或平均。

00:20:41.424 --> 00:20:57.792
In high-grade block or severe peri-arrest physiology, a drug may not provide adequate improvement and advanced electrical or perfusion support may be needed. A faster ECG without effective circulation is not a successful endpoint.
高度阻滞或严重骤停前生理时，药物可能改善不够，需高级电或灌注支持。ECG更快但循环仍无效，不是成功终点。

00:20:57.792 --> 00:21:07.536
Tachycardia may compensate for a reduced stroke volume or other stress. Rate reduction without treating that cause can make output and perfusion worse.
心动过速可能在代偿每搏量下降或其他压力，不处理病因就减速，可使心排灌注更差。

00:21:07.536 --> 00:21:22.536
Ask whether the illness preceded the rhythm or the symptoms began with it, and integrate the actual ECG and patient findings. This is reasoning under uncertainty, not a perfect history test that must delay primary support.
要问疾病先于心律，还是症状随心律开始，并结合真实ECG及患者发现。这是在不确定性下推理，不是必须延迟主要支持的完美病史测验。

00:21:22.536 --> 00:21:34.368
A rate below one hundred fifty does not guarantee safety. The type of rhythm, underlying disease and patient response matter more than assuming one universal dangerous-rate threshold.
心率低于150不保证安全。心律类型、原有病及患者反应，比假设统一危险频率阈值更重要。

00:21:34.368 --> 00:21:44.928
If effective circulation disappears, stop using the with-a-pulse pathway. State the transition clearly and begin the appropriate arrest response with the team.
若有效循环消失，就不能继续有脉搏流程。应明确宣布转换，并由团队启动适当骤停响应。

00:21:44.928 --> 00:21:57.336
The previous manual-defibrillation lesson taught the arrest shock workflow. A patient with a pulse has different electrical-treatment branches that require trained advanced authority and patient-specific decisions.
此前手动除颤课讲骤停电击，有脉搏患者则有不同电治疗分支，需要受训高级权限及患者特定决策。

00:21:57.336 --> 00:22:08.184
Synchronized cardioversion coordinates energy to a detected ventricular complex in a suitable rhythm. It is not a smaller shock that can be substituted whenever a pulse is present.
同步转复是在合适心律下，将能量与检测到的心室波群协调，不是只要有脉搏就可随意替换的小电击。

00:22:08.184 --> 00:22:21.816
Polymorphic ventricular tachycardia may not permit reliable synchronization and can require unsynchronized defibrillation. Do not delay urgent treatment trying indefinitely to obtain synchronization markers.
多形室速可能无法可靠同步，并可需要非同步除颤。不能为无限寻找同步标记延误紧急治疗。

00:22:21.816 --> 00:22:34.704
Pacing requires both electrical and mechanical assessment under the actual procedure. A spike or displayed rate is not proof of capture with effective perfusion, and this overview is not a pacing checkoff.
起搏需按实际流程同时评电及机械效果。起搏钉或显示心率不证明已有有效灌注的夺获，此概览也不等于起搏考核通过。

00:22:34.704 --> 00:22:47.328
Fluid in lung tissue or alveoli can impair gas exchange and increase breathing work. Cardiac dysfunction is important, but toxic exposure and drowning are among other causes.
肺组织或肺泡积液会损害气体交换并增加呼吸功。心功能障碍很重要，中毒暴露及溺水等也可造成。

00:22:47.328 --> 00:22:58.920
Assess the whole pattern instead of diagnosing from wheeze alone. Congestion, history, pressure and other findings can help, while mixed lung and heart disease can coexist.
不能只凭喘鸣下诊断，要看整体模式。淤血、病史、血压等有帮助，肺心混合病也可并存。

00:22:58.920 --> 00:23:13.464
A patient who cannot tolerate lying flat should not be forced flat merely for a convenient examination. At the same time, falling pressure or impaired airway protection may change the safe position and support plan.
不能只为方便检查，强迫不能耐受平卧者躺平；但血压下降或气道保护受损也会改变安全体位及支持计划。

00:23:13.464 --> 00:23:27.312
Diminishing breath size, falling awareness or an inability to maintain ventilation signals failure, not improvement. Be ready to assist ventilation effectively, especially during movement or a positional change.
呼吸变浅、意识下降或不能维持通气，提示衰竭而非好转。尤其移动和体位变化时，要准备有效辅助通气。

00:23:27.312 --> 00:23:43.512
CPAP can help selected spontaneously breathing patients, but a pulmonary-edema label does not automatically make it appropriate. Apply the actual training, indication and exclusion criteria from the earlier airway course and current procedure.
CPAP可帮助部分自主呼吸患者，但肺水肿名称不自动使它适用。需使用此前气道课及现行流程的真实训练、指征和排除条件。

00:23:43.512 --> 00:23:56.352
The checked procedure requires an awake patient able to follow commands and maintain an airway, and excludes important unsafe states. It is not a replacement for ventilation in apnea or inadequate breathing.
核对的流程要求清醒、能执行指令且维持气道，并排除重要不安全状态；它不能替代呼吸暂停或不足时所需通气。

00:23:56.352 --> 00:24:10.416
Observe work of breathing, tidal volume, alertness, oxygenation, pressure and tolerance. Positive pressure can affect venous return, so the circulation must be reassessed along with the lungs.
应观察呼吸功、潮气量、意识、氧合、血压及耐受。正压会影响回心血量，所以肺与循环都需复评。

00:24:10.416 --> 00:24:25.032
If the patient fails, change to effective BVM support and appropriate escalation rather than simply tightening a mask or raising pressure. Use a PEEP valve only when its actual procedure and patient conditions permit.
失败时要转有效BVM及适当升级，不能只勒紧面罩或加压。PEEP阀仅在真实流程和患者条件允许时使用。

00:24:25.032 --> 00:24:39.288
Obstruction can prevent filling or forward ejection even when myocardium is not the primary failure. Tamponade and major pulmonary embolism illustrate why more rate or a pain medicine may not solve the problem.
即使心肌不是主要失败，梗阻也可阻止充盈或前向射血。压塞及重大肺栓塞说明，增加心率或给止痛药未必能解决。

00:24:39.288 --> 00:24:52.632
Beck’s triad, electrical alternans or pulsus paradoxus may suggest tamponade, but their absence cannot exclude it. No single classical sign provides certainty in every patient.
Beck三联征、电交替或奇脉可提示压塞，但没有也不能排除；任何经典单征都不能对每位患者提供确定性。

00:24:52.632 --> 00:25:08.232
Combine history, breathing, perfusion and available findings, and communicate the suspected mechanism. Do not delay urgent support while searching for every classic sign or assume equal breath sounds exclude all other threats.
需结合病史、呼吸、灌注及可获发现，并传达怀疑机制。不能为找全经典征象延迟紧急支持，也不能因呼吸音相同就排除其他威胁。

00:25:08.232 --> 00:25:19.944
Definitive invasive treatment depends on the cause and advanced or surgical resources. Reading about a needle or thrombolytic does not authorize an independent PCP procedure.
确定性侵入治疗依病因及高级或外科资源而定，读到穿刺或纤溶不会授权PCP独立操作。

00:25:19.944 --> 00:25:33.528
Shock involves inadequate tissue oxygen delivery or use in context. The familiar four mechanisms help organize reasoning, but patients may have mixed disease and a normal pressure during early compensation.
休克涉及具体背景下组织氧输送或利用不足。四类机制有助推理，但患者可混合，并在早期代偿时仍有正常血压。

00:25:33.528 --> 00:25:45.000
Follow the brain, breathing, pulse and skin along with pressure. A single higher reading after treatment is not proof that organ perfusion or the underlying cause improved.
血压之外还需跟踪意识、呼吸、脉及皮肤。治疗后一次读数较高，不证明器官灌注或病因改善。

00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:57.600
Cardiogenic shock does not require a known percentage of infarcted muscle. Ischemia, rhythm, toxic effects or mechanical problems can reduce output through different pathways.
心源性休克不要求先知道多少心肌梗死。缺血、心律、毒性或机械问题可通过不同路径降低输出。

00:25:57.600 --> 00:26:11.928
Describe the likely mechanism, immediate needs and uncertainty when requesting help. The next intervention must match that reasoning and actual authority, rather than treating every shock with the same large bolus.
请求支援时，应说明可能机制、即时需要及不确定性。下一干预需符合推理及真实权限，不能所有休克都同样大推液。

00:26:11.928 --> 00:26:23.928
Dissection creates a false channel in the aortic wall; aneurysm is abnormal dilation and can leak or rupture. They are different disorders, and either can cause a time-critical patient.
夹层是在主动脉壁形成假通道，动脉瘤是异常扩张且可漏或破裂；两者不同，都可造成紧急患者。

00:26:23.928 --> 00:26:36.576
Abrupt maximal pain, syncope or neurologic and limb findings are important clues. Some patients do not have classic tearing pain, and equal arm pressures do not rule out dissection.
突发达到最重的痛、晕厥或神经肢体发现是重要线索，但有些没有典型撕裂痛，双臂血压相同也不能排除夹层。

00:26:36.576 --> 00:26:51.552
Reduce exertion, support the patient and communicate the suspicion promptly for the appropriate destination. Fluid, analgesia and pressure management require the actual cause-specific plan rather than copying the ACS pathway.
需减少用力、支持患者并尽快传达怀疑以确定适当目的地。补液、镇痛及血压管理需真实病因特定方案，不能复制ACS流程。

00:26:51.552 --> 00:27:05.928
Do not start a generic antihypertensive or chase a normal pressure independently from this reading. A leaking aneurysm is a surgical emergency, not an opportunity to finish every possible scene procedure first.
不能凭本阅读独立开通用降压药或追正常血压。渗漏动脉瘤是外科急症，不应先在现场做完所有可能操作。

00:27:05.928 --> 00:27:18.192
Pain, distress and technique can affect a pressure measurement. Repeat a sound measurement while assessing the patient, rather than diagnosing chronic hypertension from one emergency reading.
疼痛、痛苦和技术会影响血压，应在评估患者同时正确复测，不能用一次急救读数诊断慢性高血压。

00:27:18.192 --> 00:27:33.168
Hypertensive emergency involves acute target-organ injury. Neurologic change, acute pulmonary edema, ischemia and aortic disease have different treatment considerations; the number alone does not identify the pathway.
高血压急症涉及急性靶器官损伤。神经改变、急性肺水肿、缺血及主动脉病考量不同，数字本身不能确定路径。

00:27:33.168 --> 00:27:47.880
Do not apply the older textbook single MAP threshold or one-third reduction instruction as a universal field rule. Rapid indiscriminate lowering can harm perfusion, especially when a specific condition needs a different approach.
不能把旧教材单一MAP阈值或降三分之一指令当现场通用规则。快速无差别降压可损害灌注，尤其具体病需要不同方法时。

00:27:47.880 --> 00:28:00.312
Provide indicated support and timely appropriate evaluation, and communicate the actual observations and trend. Chronic follow-up and an acute emergency are distinct decisions.
应给有指征支持并及时适当评估，传达真实观察及趋势。慢性随访与急症是不同决定。

00:28:00.312 --> 00:28:13.848
A fifty-nine-year-old at a community meeting develops chest pressure and nausea. The patient is clammy, has a rate of forty-six and a pressure of eighty-six over fifty-two, and currently breathes adequately.
社区会议中一位59岁患者出现胸压和恶心，冷汗、心率46、血压86/52，目前呼吸尚足够。

00:28:13.848 --> 00:28:31.608
State the problem as suspected acute coronary ischemia with bradycardia and poor perfusion. Support immediate needs, minimize exertion, prepare equipment and appropriate resources, and obtain or preserve the useful ECG without delaying urgent care.
应表述为疑急性冠脉缺血伴过缓及低灌注。需支持即时需要、减少用力、准备器材及适当资源，并在不延误急救下取得或保留有用ECG。

00:28:31.608 --> 00:28:44.088
The nitrate screen fails. Explain pressure and rate exclusions plus possible right-sided involvement; do not give a dose merely because a family member hands you the patient’s usual spray.
硝酸酯筛查不通过。应解释血压心率排除及可能右侧受累，不能只因家属递来常用喷剂就给。

00:28:44.088 --> 00:28:59.856
Pre-alert with the timeline, inferior findings, perfusion, actual actions and response, and confirm the regional destination plan. This original exercise tests reasoning, not recall of the school patient’s age or answer wording.
预警要含时间线、下壁发现、灌注、真实行动及反应，并确认区域目的地计划。本原创练习检验推理，不是背学校患者年龄或答案措辞。

00:28:59.856 --> 00:29:14.112
First change only the pressure to one hundred sixteen while the rate remains forty-six. Nitrate is still not automatically appropriate. One improved number cannot erase the other failed criteria or right-sided concern.
先只把收缩压改为116，心率仍46。硝酸酯依然不自动适合，一个数改善不会取消其他不合条件或右侧担忧。

00:29:14.112 --> 00:29:28.512
Next keep a pulse but make the breaths shallow and awareness fall. Reassess the airway and provide effective ventilatory support with the team; a normal-looking oxygen saturation is not permission to ignore inadequate ventilation.
再保留脉搏，但呼吸浅且意识下降。需重评气道并与团队有效通气，氧饱和度看着正常也不能忽略通气不足。

00:29:28.512 --> 00:29:44.640
Then change pulse status to absent with unresponsiveness and abnormal breathing. Announce the transition and begin the arrest response, including CPR and the appropriate analysis workflow, rather than continuing a with-a-pulse medication discussion.
接着改成无脉搏、无反应及异常呼吸。应宣布转换并启动骤停响应，包括CPR及适当分析，不能继续有脉搏药物讨论。

00:29:44.640 --> 00:29:58.152
Finally restore a perfusing state in the drill. Reassess and enter the verified post-arrest pathway; do not simply return to the original chest-pain checklist as though the arrest never occurred.
最后练习中恢复有灌注状态，应复评并转入核实的骤停后流程，不能像没发生骤停一样回原胸痛清单。

00:29:58.152 --> 00:30:13.224
Document the actual history, observations and trace times, including changes and measurement limitations. Do not allow an automatic monitor event or imported vital sign to replace your assessment of effective circulation.
需记真实病史、观察及记录时间，包括变化和测量限制。不能让自动监护事件或导入生命体征取代有效循环评估。

00:30:13.224 --> 00:30:24.432
Record what was given, what was not given and why. A withheld contraindicated nitrate is a reasoned safety action, not a blank medication field that should be concealed.
要记给了什么、未给什么及原因。有禁忌而不做硝酸酯是有理由的安全行动，不是应隐瞒的药单空白。

00:30:24.432 --> 00:30:38.904
Use a concise clinical handover to transfer the current state, suspected problem, relevant background, response and tasks still needed. Tell the receiving team about recurrent symptoms or deterioration during the journey.
简明交接当前状态、怀疑问题、相关背景、反应及仍需任务，途中症状复发或恶化也要告知接收团队。

00:30:38.904 --> 00:30:49.368
Confirm the handover and maintain observation until responsibility transfers appropriately. The pre-alert starts coordination; it does not end your patient care.
需确认交接，并在责任适当转移前维持观察。预警开始协调，不会结束你的患者照护。

00:30:49.368 --> 00:31:35.256
The actual first range includes the opening of 17.4. Potassium-channel effects can prolong repolarization and QT, while the QT itself also changes with heart rate. QTc is a rate-corrected estimate using a named formula; the chapter mentions Bazett, but no formula or one automatic monitor number removes the need to assess the tracing, rate, medicines and patient. Amiodarone has effects across several channel/receptor groups and can persist long after chronic therapy stops. A long elimination time is not permission to confuse its arrest push with a perfusing-rhythm infusion. This boundary does not assign every later class-III drug table.
实际第一段范围含17.4开头。钾通道作用可延长复极及QT，而QT本身也随心率改变。QTc是用特定公式校正心率的估计，教材提到Bazett；但任何公式或监护仪自动数值，都不能代替核查波形、心率、药物与患者。胺碘酮作用跨多个通道受体，长期治疗停后还可持续存在。消除慢不允许混淆骤停推注与有灌注心律输注。这个边界不等于指定全部后续III类药表。

00:31:35.256 --> 00:32:23.568
The final assigned page opens 22.3, moving from cardiac drugs to shock. In anaphylaxis, airway narrowing and vasodilation can impair oxygen delivery together. Epinephrine supports bronchial and vascular responses through different receptors; the hospital text mentioning IM or IV does not make those routes freely interchangeable. Current E09 uses IM epinephrine first for systemic anaphylaxis and reserves IV treatment for the relevant advanced refractory pathway. There are no absolute epinephrine contraindications in life-threatening anaphylaxis in the current monograph. An arrest-dose IV bolus is not the dose to copy into a patient who still has a pulse.
指定末页开始22.3，从心脏药转向休克。过敏反应中，气道缩窄与血管舒张可共同损害氧输送；肾上腺素经不同受体支持支气管及血管反应。医院文字列IM或IV，不表示两条途径可任意互换。现行E09对全身过敏反应先用IM肾上腺素，IV用于相应高级、难治路径；现行专论对危及生命过敏反应列无绝对禁忌。有脉搏患者不能照搬骤停静脉推注剂量。

00:32:23.568 --> 00:33:09.072
Translate the ending monitoring list into parallel care: reassess breathing effort, air entry, saturation, pressure, consciousness, ECG where available and the clinical response, with rescue equipment ready. Do not delay indicated IM epinephrine while obtaining a perfect monitor setup. Ask a conscious patient to report better or worse breathing or other change; inability to report makes observation more important. The next albuterol heading begins but continues beyond the assigned page. Salbutamol can support persistent bronchospasm after epinephrine in the current pathway; it does not replace epinephrine or correct the entire anaphylactic circulation problem.
把末尾监测清单转成并行照护：复评呼吸用力、进气、饱和度、血压、意识、可用时ECG及临床反应，并备好救援器械。不能为了完美监护配置而延误有指征IM肾上腺素。清醒患者应报告呼吸或其他变化是好是坏，不能报告时更需观察。后续albuterol标题虽已开始，正文续在指定页之外。现行路径中沙丁胺醇可在肾上腺素后支持持续支气管痉挛，却不能替代肾上腺素或纠正整个过敏循环问题。

00:33:09.072 --> 00:33:56.736
Follow the medication through an error-sensitive chain: prescribing, transcription, dispensing, preparation, administration, monitoring and recording. A complete instruction includes the correct patient, generic or verified product name, dose with units, necessary strength or concentration, route, timing, indication and valid prescriber or protocol authority. Date, time and authentication matter for a written or verbal order. A chemical name describes structure, a generic name identifies the active agent and a brand identifies a marketed product; none alone proves the formulation. Resolve an incomplete order before giving it, even when the drug cabinet or computer accepted it.
沿容易出错的链追踪药物：开立、转录、调配、准备、给药、监测及记录。完整指令应有正确患者、通用名或已核实产品名、带单位剂量、必要强度浓度、途径、时间、指征，以及有效处方者或规程权限；书面和口头指令的日期、时间及认证都重要。化学名描述结构，通用名识别活性药物，商品名识别上市产品，任一名称单独都不证明剂型。即使药柜或电脑已接受，指令不完整也应先解决再给。

00:33:56.736 --> 00:34:55.824
Decode a route without silently choosing it. PO, SL and buccal refer to oral, under-tongue and cheek placement; PR and PV refer to rectal and vaginal routes. IM, IV, IV push, IV piggyback, SC or SQ and ID name different tissue or vascular routes. Inhaled, nasal, topical, transdermal and nasogastric delivery are also different. The source uses AD/AS/AU for ears and OD/OS/OU for eyes; ambiguous shorthand is unsafe. Its EPI entry means epidural, not automatically epinephrine, while IA, IC and IT mean intra-arterial, intracardiac and intrathecal. Recognizing those labels is not permission to use the route. Clarify unfamiliar abbreviations and write the actual medicine and route clearly.
辨认途径时不能暗自替患者选择：PO、SL及buccal分别指口服、舌下和颊部；PR、PV为直肠和阴道。IM、IV、静脉推注、静脉间歇输注、SC或SQ及ID指不同组织或血管途径。吸入、鼻内、外涂、透皮及鼻胃管也不同。来源用AD、AS、AU表示耳，OD、OS、OU表示眼；含糊缩写不安全。其EPI条目指硬膜外，不自动等于肾上腺素；IA、IC、IT为动脉内、心内及鞘内。认识名称不授权使用途径，应澄清不熟悉缩写，清楚写真实药物及途径。

00:34:55.824 --> 00:35:30.360
Use a medicine name as a clue, then verify the actual product. Metoprolol is a beta blocker, lisinopril is an ACE inhibitor, and losartan is an angiotensin receptor blocker. Those are different ways to influence the circulation, not interchangeable tablets for a low or high pressure. The bilingual reader gives the longer spelling reference. In the weekly case, explain what the confirmed medicine could change in rate, contraction, filling, resistance or potassium, and check the patient rather than selecting a drug from its ending.
药名可作线索，但随后须核实真实产品。美托洛尔是β阻滞剂，赖诺普利是ACE抑制剂，氯沙坦是血管紧张素受体阻滞剂；它们以不同方式影响循环，不是遇高低血压可互换的片剂。双语阅读提供更长的拼写参考。本周病例中，应解释已确认药物可能怎样改变频率、收缩、充盈、阻力或钾，并评估患者，不能从词尾选药。

00:35:30.360 --> 00:36:10.008
The remaining reference groups medicines for infection, inflammation, allergy, airway narrowing, pain, seizures, sleep and mental health. Recognizing a family helps anticipate questions about effects and interactions, but it does not establish the exact medicine, approved indication, formulation, route or dose. Some matching name endings have important exceptions. Two medicines affecting one organ may be intentionally prescribed together. Compare the real plan and the reason for each treatment instead of declaring every such combination an error or turning the reference table into a medication order.
其余参考把感染、炎症、过敏、气道缩窄、疼痛、癫痫、睡眠及精神健康用药分组。认识家族有助预想药效和相互作用问题，却不能确认具体药物、批准指征、剂型、途径或剂量；相同词尾存在重要例外。影响同一器官的两种药可能有意合用。应比较真实计划及各治疗目的，不能把每种这类组合都判错，也不能把参考表变成用药指令。

00:36:10.008 --> 00:36:54.624
Action and indication answer different questions: how the drug works versus why it is prescribed. Beta blockers reduce receptor responses; they do not simply stop adrenaline being released. Diuretics can change renal salt and water handling and reduce circulating volume, so the patient with bradycardia and falling pressure needs more than a medicine-name checklist. An FDA-labelled or off-label example is U.S. regulatory context, not a BC paramedic authority statement. Compare the real indication, interactions and expected response. The source statement that twice daily automatically means every twelve hours must not override the actual prescribed schedule.
作用与指征回答不同问题：药如何起效，以及为何开给患者。β阻滞剂减少受体反应，不是简单阻止肾上腺素释放；利尿剂可改变肾脏盐水处理并减少循环量，所以慢心率且血压下降者不能只核药名。FDA批准或超说明书例子是美国监管背景，不是BC救护权限声明。应比较真实指征、相互作用及预期反应；来源说每天两次自动等于每12小时，不能覆盖真实规定时间表。

00:36:54.624 --> 00:37:38.184
Build the safe environment around the high-alert medicine. Keep products secure, prepare for one identified patient at a time, label every prepared container and protect against interruptions, loss and accidental reuse. Do not put an unidentified syringe or patient medicine in a pocket. Tall Man lettering highlights risky differences, such as DOPamine versus DOBUTamine or hydrALAZINE versus hydrOXYzine; it is not an identity check by itself. An independent second check and a read-back address different errors. Apply the actual agency storage, controlled-drug accounting and documentation process rather than importing a U.S. ward rule as BC law.
围绕高警示药建立安全环境：妥善保管，一次为一名已确认患者准备，标记每个已准备容器，并防干扰、遗失及误重复使用。不要把不明针筒或患者药放口袋。Tall Man大小写突出易混差异，例如DOPamine与DOBUTamine、hydrALAZINE与hydrOXYzine，但不单独完成身份核对。独立第二核查与回读针对不同错误。应依真实机构保管、管制药核账及记录流程，不把美国病房规则当BC法律。

00:37:38.184 --> 00:38:32.064
Separate an expected side effect, an unwanted adverse reaction, immune allergy, excessive toxic exposure, tolerance, interaction and an apparently opposite response. They are not interchangeable allergy labels. Tolerance means a weaker response after repeated exposure; it is not the same as physical dependence or addiction and does not authorize a self-selected dose increase. A new symptom could instead be worsening disease, a wrong product or a delivery error. Support immediate threats, assess the actual reaction and report facts and timing. Finish 11.1 with history/assessment, interaction checks, understandable education and the informed refusal process under the real consent framework. The source note about U.S. parental rights is not automatically a BC rule.
应区分预期副作用、不良反应、免疫过敏、过量毒性暴露、耐受、相互作用及表面相反反应，不能全贴成过敏。耐受指重复暴露后反应变弱，不同于身体依赖或成瘾，也不授权自行加量；新症状还可能是病情恶化、给错产品或输注错误。应支持即时威胁、评估实际反应，并报告事实时间。11.1末尾还需病史评估、相互作用核查、可理解教育及真实同意框架下的知情拒绝流程。来源美国父母权利注释不自动成为BC规则。

00:38:32.064 --> 00:39:17.616
The literal 18.4 pages add selected cardiopulmonary support to the examination. Diaphragmatic and pursed-lip techniques may help a cooperative patient control breathing, while coughing, deep breaths, incentive spirometry, repositioning and appropriate mobility support selected ongoing-care plans. An incentive spirometer is an inhalation exercise device, not an oxygen source or a rescue ventilator. Do not label severe breathlessness as anxiety or delay airway/perfusion support while coaching. Evaluate the patient, the indication, technique and response; an anecdote about a postoperative patient is not a universal prescription for a near-arrest patient.
字面18.4页在检查之外加入特定心肺支持。膈式及缩唇技巧可帮助能配合者控制呼吸；咳嗽、深呼吸、激励肺量计、变换体位及适当活动用于特定持续照护计划。激励肺量计是吸气训练器，不是氧源或救援呼吸机。不能把严重气促贴成焦虑，也不能为练呼吸而延误气道灌注支持。应评患者、指征、技术及反应，术后患者故事不是接近骤停者的通用处方。

00:39:17.616 --> 00:40:06.072
Connect the medication tables to mechanisms already taught this week. Bronchodilators relax airway smooth muscle; anti-inflammatory treatment is different from immediate bronchodilation, secretion-modifying drugs differ from cough suppression, and antimicrobials require an appropriate infection indication. Cardiac drugs may alter rate, conduction, contraction, loading, lipids or thrombosis. A beta blocker does not automatically have amiodarone-like class-III effects; an anticoagulant does not directly replace an antiplatelet. Compare the actual product and contraindications, then observe ventilation and perfusion. The hospital table is not a set of additional independent PCP medication permissions.
把药表连到本周已学机制：支气管舒张药放松气道平滑肌，抗炎不同于即时舒张，改变分泌物不同于抑咳，抗微生物药需合适感染指征。心脏药可影响频率、传导、收缩、负荷、血脂或血栓。β阻滞剂不自动具有胺碘酮样III类作用，抗凝也不直接替代抗血小板。应比较真实产品及禁忌，再观察通气和灌注。医院药表不构成额外PCP独立用药权限。

00:40:06.072 --> 00:40:55.176
Choose oxygen delivery by the actual need and device, not a promise of one exact percentage. The source tables give nasal-cannula, simple-mask, reservoir-mask and higher-support examples; flow and inspired concentration depend on fit, design and patient breathing. Conventional oxygen does not provide a breath to an apneic patient. High-flow nasal systems, noninvasive positive pressure, a bag-mask and an invasive ventilator are not interchangeable. Use the separately labelled current target, observe breathing/pressure and reassess. A patient with COPD is not automatically denied needed oxygen, and a high saturation does not establish adequate ventilation or cardiac output.
应按真实需要和器械选氧输送，不能承诺固定百分比。来源表有鼻导管、简单面罩、储氧面罩及更高级支持例子，流量和吸入浓度受贴合、设计及患者呼吸影响。普通氧疗不能为无呼吸者提供一口气，高流量鼻系统、无创正压、球囊面罩及有创呼吸机也不能互换。应使用另行标示的现行目标，观察呼吸和血压并复评。COPD不自动成为拒绝必要氧气的理由，高饱和度也不证明通气或心排充分。

00:40:55.176 --> 00:41:44.208
Understand what the hospital interventions change. A chest drain removes pleural air or fluid through a prescribed system; it is not a reason to clamp or disconnect a transferred drain routinely. Electrical cardioversion, arrest defibrillation, pacing and airway/ventilator support have different purposes and authorization. After movement or an intervention, recheck the patient and the actual connections, delivery and response. Mechanical ventilation introduces infection, pressure and sedation-related considerations. The source recommendation about a proton-pump inhibitor preventing ventilator-associated pneumonia must not become routine VAP prophylaxis: stress-ulcer prevention and pneumonia prevention are different decisions.
应理解医院干预改变什么：胸腔引流经规定系统移除胸膜腔气或液，不意味着转运时常规夹闭断开。电复律、骤停除颤、起搏及气道呼吸机支持有不同目的与权限。移动或干预后，应重查患者、实际连接、输送和反应。有创通气带来感染、压力及镇静等考量。来源关于质子泵抑制剂防呼吸机相关肺炎的建议，不能变成常规VAP预防；应激性溃疡预防与肺炎预防是不同决定。

00:41:44.208 --> 00:42:35.088
Finish the management pages with continuity, not just machinery. Explain the actual care plan, use teach-back and include the patient preferences and relevant supporters. Smoking/pollutant exposure, nutrition, energy conservation, cardiac rehabilitation, coping and comfort need individualized plans and appropriate team members. Chest physiotherapy or postural drainage is not an automatic response to every crackle, and diet counselling cannot displace immediate stabilization. In the weekly slow, hypotensive chest-pain case, describe the treatment purpose and a patient-level response, identify an adverse change and hand over what was actually done. This links the medication-rights, cardiopulmonary-management and cardiovascular-assessment readings into one encounter.
管理页最后要接上连续照护，不只是机器：解释真实计划、用复述确认理解，纳入患者偏好及相关支持者。吸烟污染暴露、营养、节能、心脏康复、应对与舒适，需要个体计划及适当团队。胸部物理治疗或体位引流不是一听湿啰音就自动做，饮食教育也不能挤掉即时稳定。本周慢脉低血压胸痛病例中，应描述治疗目的及患者层面反应、识别不良变化，并交接实际所做，把给药原则、心肺管理及心血管评估读成一次完整接触。

00:42:35.088 --> 00:42:46.920
Explain one whole encounter from first contact to the receiving team. Start with immediate threats and show how the history, observations and ECG change your next actions.
请从首次接触到接收团队讲一个完整过程。先即时威胁，再展示病史、观察及ECG怎样改变下一行动。

00:42:46.920 --> 00:42:59.904
Explain the Nitro Trap through venous return and the serial circuit, then state the actual pressure, rate and other screening failures. Do not reduce it to a slogan that all inferior infarcts are the same.
先用回心血量及串联循环解释Nitro Trap，再说真实血压、心率及其他不合条件，不能缩成所有下壁梗死一样的口号。

00:42:59.904 --> 00:43:13.392
Separate source differences and operator authority from physiology. You should understand advanced treatments well enough to recognize and assist appropriately without claiming permissions that the course does not grant.
把来源差异、操作者权限与生理区分。应理解高级治疗到能识别并适当协助，但不能声称课程给予了没有的权限。

00:43:13.392 --> 00:43:24.792
Use the bilingual CNS, PHARM and Nancy reading below to reconstruct the reasoning, then practise the original questions and move into the integrated weekend team rehearsal.
可用下方中英对照CNS、PHARM及Nancy阅读重建推理，再练原创问题，随后进入周末团队整合演练。
